# FABLE-SONNET-DECL-PREPASS-20260923-137 part 2, restated by the call rule (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-20260929-16):
# b is an EXISTING Model value, and a named Structure value is callable, so `b: same(a)` is b's call with same(a)'s
# result as its argument -- refused where it stands until a named Structure's call with an argument is built.  (It
# reached the typed-typed graph rebinding's fail-closed "graph assignment admission requires receiving-expression
# tests".)  The explicit reference place is unit_struct_return_ref_admit_refused.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

fn: same (Model: x) Model
    return: x
end: same

fn: probe () int
    a: merge: Model
    b: merge: Model
    b: same(a)
    return: 0
end: probe

return: probe()
